{"qid": "gf-10", "paper_id": "2001.06899", "answer": true, "unanimous": true, "quote": "The missing transverse momentum vector, ${\\vec{p}}_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\kern 1.0pt\text{miss}}$ , is computed as the negative vector sum of the transverse momenta of all PF candidates in an event [ 41 ] and is further modified to account for corrections to the energy scale of the reconstructed jets. Its magnitude, $p_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\text{miss}}$ , is required to be less than 40  GeV , which results in a signal efficiency of ${\\approx}80\\%$ with the $\\mathup{{{t}}}$ $\\mathup{{\\overline{{{\\mathup{{{t}}}}}}}}$ rejection factor of ${\\approx}4.8$ .", "all_quotes": ["The missing transverse momentum vector, ${\\vec{p}}_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\kern 1.0pt\text{miss}}$ , is computed as the negative vector sum of the transverse momenta of all PF candidates in an event [ 41 ] and is further modified to account for corrections to the energy scale of the reconstructed jets. Its magnitude, $p_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\text{miss}}$ , is required to be less than 40  GeV , which results in a signal efficiency of ${\\approx}80\\%$ with the $\\mathup{{{t}}}$ $\\mathup{{\\overline{{{\\mathup{{{t}}}}}}}}$ rejection factor of ${\\approx}4.8$ .", "The missing transverse momentum vector, ${\\vec{p}}_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\kern 1.0pt\text{miss}}$ , is computed as the negative vector sum of the transverse momenta of all PF candidates in an event and is further modified to account for corrections to the energy scale of the reconstructed jets. Its magnitude, $p_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\text{miss}}$ , is required to be less than 40  GeV , which results in a signal efficiency of ${\\approx}80\\%$ with the $\\mathup{{{t}}}$ $\\mathup{{\\overline{{{\\mathup{{{t}}}}}}}}$ rejection factor of ${\\approx}4.8$ .", "Missing transverse momentum selection efficiency: This uncertainty source accounts for possible differences in the $p_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\text{miss}}$ selection ( $p_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\text{miss}}<40\\,\text{Ge\\hskip-0.80002ptV}$ ) efficiencies for ${\\mathup{{{Z}}}}\\hskip-2.5pt+\\hskip-1.49994pt\text{jets}$ and ${\\mathup{{{Z}}}}\\hskip-2.5pt+\\hskip-1.49994pt\text{HF~jets}$ events.", "Therefore, the efficiencies tend to be lower for ${\\mathup{{{Z}}}}\\hskip-2.5pt+\\hskip-1.49994pt\text{HF~jets}$ events by ${\\approx}1\\%$ at high jet and $\\mathup{{{Z}}}$ boson $p_{\\mathrm{T}}$ regions compared to those of ${\\mathup{{{Z}}}}\\hskip-2.5pt+\\hskip-1.49994pt\text{jets}$ events."], "answers": ["The pT^miss < 40 GeV cut has an efficiency that is lower for ${\\mathup{{{Z}}}}\\hskip-2.5pt+\\hskip-1.49994pt\text{HF~jets}$ events by approximately 1% at high jet and $\\mathup{{{Z}}}$ boson $p_{\\mathrm{T}}$ regions compared to those of ${\\mathup{{{Z}}}}\\hskip-2.5pt+\\hskip-1.49994pt\text{jets}$ events.", "The pT^miss < 40 GeV cut results in a signal efficiency of approximately 80%.", "The pT^miss < 40 GeV cut retains a signal efficiency of approximately 80%.", "The signal efficiency of the pT^miss < 40 GeV cut is approximately 80%.", "The text mentions the pT^miss < 40 GeV cut and its efficiency, but does not specify the signal efficiency retained by this cut."], "votes": {"False": 25, "True": 5}, "escalated": false, "sections_read": [" + Abstract + Introduction + The CMS detector + Data and simulated samples", "Appendix B Measured differential cross section ratios", "Cross section ratio measurements + Analysis strategy + $\\mathup{{{Z}}}$ +HF jets event tagging efficiency", "Estimation of the event yields", "Object reconstruction and event selection", "Results + Summary + Appendix A Post-fit $M_{\\text{SV}}$ distributions in the exclusive jet $p_{\\mathrm{T}}$ bins", "Systematic uncertainties", "Unfolding"], "verdicts": [{"paper_id": "2001.06899", "qid": "gf-10", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Abstract + Introduction + The CMS detector + Data and simulated samples", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\