up{{{t}}}}}}}}$ rejection factor of ${\\approx}4.8$ .", "quote_verified": true, "quotes": ["The missing transverse momentum vector, ${\\vec{p}}_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\kern 1.0pt\text{miss}}$ , is computed as the negative vector sum of the transverse momenta of all PF candidates in an event and is further modified to account for corrections to the energy scale of the reconstructed jets. Its magnitude, $p_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\text{miss}}$ , is required to be less than 40  GeV , which results in a signal efficiency of ${\\approx}80\\%$ with the $\\mathup{{{t}}}$ $\\mathup{{\\overline{{{\\mathup{{{t}}}}}}}}$ rejection factor of ${\\approx}4.8$ ."], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "The signal efficiency of the pT^miss < 40 GeV cut is approximately 80%.", "section": "Object reconstruction and event selection", "window": 1, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The question asks for the signal efficiency of the pT^miss < 40 GeV cut. The text discusses the pT^miss cut and its efficiency.\",\n  \"quotes\": [\n    \"The missing transverse momentum vector, ${\\vec{p}}_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\kern 1.0pt\\text{miss}}$ , is computed as the negative vector sum of the transverse momenta of all PF candidates in an event and is further modified to account for corrections to the energy scale of the reconstructed jets. Its magnitude, $p_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\text{miss}}$ , is required to be less than 40  GeV , which results in a signal efficiency of ${\\approx}80\\%$ with the $\\mathup{{{t}}}$ $\\mathup{{\\overline{{{\\mathup{{{t}}}}}}}}$ rejection factor of ${\\approx}4.8$ .\"\n  ],\n  \"answer\": \"The signal efficiency of the pT^miss < 40 GeV cut is approximately 80%.\",\n  \"found\": true\n}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2001.06899", "qid": "gf-10", "answer": true, "quote": "Missing transverse momentum is used in this analysis to reduce background contributions from $\\mathup{{{t}}}$ $\\mathup{{\\overline{{{\\mathup{{{t}}}}}}}}$ and single top quark production processes. In contrast to the ${\\mathup{{{Z}}}}\\hskip-2.5pt+\\hskip-1.49994pt\text{jets}$ , these processes have a significant amount of missing energy because of undetected neutrinos in top quark decays. The missing transverse momentum vector, ${\\vec{p}}_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\kern 1.0pt\text{miss}}$ , is computed as the negative vector sum of the transverse momenta of all PF candidates in an event [ 41 ] and is further modified to account for corrections to the energy scale of the reconstructed jets. Its magnitude, $p_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\text{miss}}$ , is required to be less than 40  GeV , which results in a signal efficiency of ${\\approx}80\\%$ with the $\\mathup{{{t}}}$ $\\mathup{{\\overline{{{\\mathup{{{t}}}}}}}}$ rejection factor of ${\\approx}4.8$ .", "quote_verified": true, "quotes": ["Missing transverse momentum is used in this analysis to reduce background contributions from $\\mathup{{{t}}}$ $\\mathup{{\\overline{{{\\mathup{{{t}}}}}}}}$ and single top quark production processes. In contrast to the ${\\mathup{{{Z}}}}\\hskip-2.5pt+\\hskip-1.49994pt\text{jets}$ , these processes have a significant amount of missing energy because of undetected neutrinos in top quark decays. The missing transverse momentum vector, ${\\vec{p}}_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\kern 1.0pt\text{miss}}$ , is computed as the negative vector sum of the transverse momenta of all PF candidates in an event [ 41 ] and is further modified to account for corrections to the energy scale of the reconstructed jets. Its magnitude, $p_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\text{miss}}$ , is required to be less than 40  GeV , which results in a signal efficiency of ${\\approx}80\\%$ with the $\\mathup{{{t}}}$ $\\mathup{{\\overline{{{\\mathup{{{t}}}}}}}}$ rejection factor of ${\\approx}4.8$ ."], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "The pT^miss < 40 GeV cut results in a signal efficiency of approximately 80%.", "section": "Object reconstruction and event selection", "window": 1, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The question asks about the signal efficiency of the pT^miss < 40 GeV cut. The text discusses the pT^miss cut and its efficiency.\",\n  \"quotes\": [\n    \"Missing transverse momentum is used in this analysis to reduce background contributions from $\\mathup{{{t}}}$ $\\mathup{{\\overline{{{\\mathup{{{t}}}}}}}}$ and single top quark production processes. In contrast to the ${\\mathup{{{Z}}}}\\hskip-2.5pt+\\hskip-1.49994pt\\text{jets}$ , these processes have a significant amount of missing energy because of undetected neutrinos in top quark decays. The missing transverse momentum vector, ${\\vec{p}}_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\kern 1.0pt\\text{miss}}$ , is computed as the negative vector sum of the transverse momenta of all PF candidates in an event [ 41 ] and is further modified to account for corrections to the energy scale of the reconstructed jets. Its magnitude, $p_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\text{miss}}$ , is required to be less than 40  GeV , which results in a signal efficiency of ${\\approx}80\\%$ with the $\\mathup{{{t}}}$ $\\mathup{{\\overline{{{\\mathup{{{t}}}}}}}}$ rejection factor of ${\\approx}4.8$ .\"\n  ],\n  \"answer\": \"The pT^miss < 40 GeV cut results in a signal efficiency of approximately 80%.\",\n  \"found\": true\n}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2001.06899", "qid": "gf-10", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Object reconstruction and event selection", "window": 2, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The text does not mention the signal efficiency of the pT^miss < 40 GeV cut.\",\n  \"quotes\": [],\n  \"answer\": \"\",\n  \"found\": false\n}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2001.06899", "qid": "gf-10", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Object reconstruction and event selection", "window": 2, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The text does not mention the signal efficiency of the pT^miss < 40 GeV cut.\",\n  \"quot