nal efficiency or the pT^miss < 40 GeV cut.\",\n  \"quotes\": [],\n  \"answer\": \"\",\n  \"found\": false\n}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2001.06899", "qid": "gf-10", "answer": true, "quote": "Missing transverse momentum selection efficiency: This uncertainty source accounts for possible differences in the $p_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\text{miss}}$ selection ( $p_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\text{miss}}<40\\,\text{Ge\\hskip-0.80002ptV}$ ) efficiencies for ${\\mathup{{{Z}}}}\\hskip-2.5pt+\\hskip-1.49994pt\text{jets}$ and ${\\mathup{{{Z}}}}\\hskip-2.5pt+\\hskip-1.49994pt\text{HF~jets}$ events.", "quote_verified": true, "quotes": ["Missing transverse momentum selection efficiency: This uncertainty source accounts for possible differences in the $p_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\text{miss}}$ selection ( $p_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\text{miss}}<40\\,\text{Ge\\hskip-0.80002ptV}$ ) efficiencies for ${\\mathup{{{Z}}}}\\hskip-2.5pt+\\hskip-1.49994pt\text{jets}$ and ${\\mathup{{{Z}}}}\\hskip-2.5pt+\\hskip-1.49994pt\text{HF~jets}$ events.", "Therefore, the efficiencies tend to be lower for ${\\mathup{{{Z}}}}\\hskip-2.5pt+\\hskip-1.49994pt\text{HF~jets}$ events by ${\\approx}1\\%$ at high jet and $\\mathup{{{Z}}}$ boson $p_{\\mathrm{T}}$ regions compared to those of ${\\mathup{{{Z}}}}\\hskip-2.5pt+\\hskip-1.49994pt\text{jets}$ events."], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "The pT^miss < 40 GeV cut has an efficiency that is lower for ${\\mathup{{{Z}}}}\\hskip-2.5pt+\\hskip-1.49994pt\text{HF~jets}$ events by approximately 1% at high jet and $\\mathup{{{Z}}}$ boson $p_{\\mathrm{T}}$ regions compared to those of ${\\mathup{{{Z}}}}\\hskip-2.5pt+\\hskip-1.49994pt\text{jets}$ events.", "section": "Systematic uncertainties", "window": 7, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The text mentions a cut on missing transverse momentum (pT^miss) and discusses the efficiency of this cut.\",\n  \"quotes\": [\n    \"Missing transverse momentum selection efficiency: This uncertainty source accounts for possible differences in the $p_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\text{miss}}$ selection ( $p_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\\text{miss}}<40\\,\\text{Ge\\hskip-0.80002ptV}$ ) efficiencies for ${\\mathup{{{Z}}}}\\hskip-2.5pt+\\hskip-1.49994pt\\text{jets}$ and ${\\mathup{{{Z}}}}\\hskip-2.5pt+\\hskip-1.49994pt\\text{HF~jets}$ events.\",\n    \"Therefore, the efficiencies tend to be lower for ${\\mathup{{{Z}}}}\\hskip-2.5pt+\\hskip-1.49994pt\\text{HF~jets}$ events by ${\\approx}1\\%$ at high jet and $\\mathup{{{Z}}}$ boson $p_{\\mathrm{T}}$ regions compared to those of ${\\mathup{{{Z}}}}\\hskip-2.5pt+\\hskip-1.49994pt\\text{jets}$ events.\"\n  ],\n  \"answer\": \"The pT^miss < 40 GeV cut has an efficiency that is lower for ${\\mathup{{{Z}}}}\\hskip-2.5pt+\\hskip-1.49994pt\\text{HF~jets}$ events by approximately 1% at high jet and $\\mathup{{{Z}}}$ boson $p_{\\mathrm{T}}$ regions compared to those of ${\\mathup{{{Z}}}}\\hskip-2.5pt+\\hskip-1.49994pt\\text{jets}$ events.\",\n  \"found\": true\n}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2001.06899", "qid": "gf-10", "answer": true, "quote": "Missing transverse momentum selection efficiency: This uncertainty source accounts for possible differences in the $p_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\text{miss}}$ selection ( $p_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\text{miss}}<40\\,\text{Ge\\hskip-0.80002ptV}$ ) efficiencies for ${\\mathup{{{Z}}}}\\hskip-2.5pt+\\hskip-1.49994pt\text{jets}$ and ${\\mathup{{{Z}}}}\\hskip-2.5pt+\\hskip-1.49994pt\text{HF~jets}$ events.", "quote_verified": true, "quotes": ["Missing transverse momentum selection efficiency: This uncertainty source accounts for possible differences in the $p_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\text{miss}}$ selection ( $p_{\\mathrm{T}}^{\text{miss}}<40\\,\text{Ge\\hskip-0.80002ptV}$ ) efficiencies for ${\\mathup{{{Z}}}}\\hskip-2.5pt+\\hskip-1.49994pt\text{jets}$ and ${\\mathup{{{Z}}}}\\hskip-2.5pt+\\hskip-1.49994pt\text{HF~jets}$ events."], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "The text mentions the pT^miss < 40 GeV cut and its efficiency, but does not specify the signal efficiency retained by this cut.", "section": "S