erified": true, "quotes": ["The observed number of events and expected yields are shown in Tables 10 and 11 for each of the inclusive 3 ℓ and 1 ℓ SRs, respectively.", "Table 10 also shows upper limits (at the 95% CL) on the number of BSM events S95 , and on the visible BSM cross-section σvis=Sobs95/∫Ldt , defined as the product of the production cross-section, acceptance and efficiency."], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "The observed number of events in SR^Z_1A is 3. The expected yield of SM events in SR^Z_1A is 5.7 ± 1.0. The upper limit on the number of BSM events (S95) in SR^Z_1A is 4.5. The expected number of BSM events given the expected number of background events (Sexp95) in SR^Z_1A is 6.2+2.6−1.6.", "section": "Results", "window": 7, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The text provides information about observed and expected yields in various signal regions, including SR^Z_1A.\",\n  \"quotes\": [\n    \"The observed number of events and expected yields are shown in Tables 10 and 11 for each of the inclusive 3 ℓ and 1 ℓ SRs, respectively.\",\n    \"Table 10 also shows upper limits (at the 95% CL) on the number of BSM events S95 , and on the visible BSM cross-section σvis=Sobs95/∫Ldt , defined as the product of the production cross-section, acceptance and efficiency.\",\n    \"SR Z1A Observed events 3 Total (post-fit) SM events 5.7 ± 1.0\",\n    \"SR Z1A Sobs95 4.5\",\n    \"SR Z1A Sexp95 6.2+2.6−1.6\"\n  ],\n  \"answer\": \"The observed number of events in SR^Z_1A is 3. The expected yield of SM events in SR^Z_1A is 5.7 ± 1.0. The upper limit on the number of BSM events (S95) in SR^Z_1A is 4.5. The expected number of BSM events given the expected number of background events (Sexp95) in SR^Z_1A is 6.2+2.6−1.6.\",\n  \"found\": true\n}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2006.05880", "qid": "gf-15", "answer": true, "quote": "The observed number of events and expected yields are shown in Tables 10 and 11 for each of the inclusive 3 ℓ and 1 ℓ SRs, respe