"window": 21, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The text does not mention any yields in SR^Z_1A of 2006.05880.\",\n  \"quotes\": [],\n  \"answer\": \"\",\n  \"found\": false\n}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2006.05880", "qid": "gf-15", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "", "window": 22, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The text does not mention the observed and expected yields in SR^Z_1A of 2006.05880.\",\n  \"quotes\": [],\n  \"answer\": \"\",\n  \"found\": false\n}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2006.05880", "qid": "gf-15", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "", "window": 22, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The text does not mention observed or expected yields in SR^Z_1A.\",\n  \"quotes\": [],\n  \"answer\": \"\",\n  \"found\": false\n}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2006.05880", "qid": "gf-15", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "", "window": 22, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The text does not mention SR^Z_1A or any yields related to it.\",\n  \"quotes\": [],\n  \"answer\": \"\",\n  \"found\": false\n}\n```"}]}
{"qid": "gf-11", "paper_id": "2001.06899", "answer": true, "unanimous": false, "quote": "The discrimination of HF jets from light-flavor quark and gluon jets, referred to as light jets in the following, is achieved by constructing a discriminator variable from tracks and secondary vertex (SV) characteristics. Artificial neural network algorithms are used to combine specific properties of the HF quarks, long lifetime and substantial mass, to build the discriminator. The algorithm used in the analysis, the combined secondary vertex (Version 2), is described in Ref. [ 42 ] .", "all_quotes": ["The discrimination of HF jets from light-flavor quark and gluon jets, referred to as light jets in the following, is achieved by constructing a discriminator variable from tracks and secondary vertex (SV) characteristics. Artificial neural network algorithms are used to combine specific properties of the HF quarks, long lifetime and substantial mass, to build the discriminator. The algorithm used in the analysis, the combined secondary vertex (Version 2), is described in Ref. [ 42 ] .", "The analysis uses a “medium” operating point, which corresponds to approximately 10 (60)% tagging efficiencies for $\\mathup{{{c}}}$ ( $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ ) quark jets and a misidentification probability of 1% for a light jet.", "The jet HF tagging requirement described in Section 4.", "The scale factors obtained from the combined fit in the inclusive ${\\mathup{{{Z}}}}\\hskip-2.5pt+\\hskip-1.49994pt\text{HF~jets}$ data sample are $\text{SF}_{\text{c}}=0.849\\pm 0.013\text{ (stat)}\\pm 0.064\text{ (syst)}$ and $\text{SF}_{\text{b}}=0.873\\pm 0.005\text{ (stat)}\\pm 0.013\text{ (syst)}$.", "Heavy-flavor tagging efficiency: The HF tagging efficiencies for $\\mathup{{{c}}}$ and $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ jets are estimated in simulation and corrected by the efficiency scale factors as described in Section 5.2 . The systematic uncertainties of the efficiency scale factors of $\\mathup{{{c}}}$ jets and $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ jets with $30<p_{\\mathrm{T}}<100\\,\\text{Ge\\hskip-0.80002ptV}$ and $\\lvert\\eta\\rvert<2.4$ are ${\\approx}3.5\\%$ and ${\\approx}1.4\\%$ , respectively [ 42 ] ."], "answers": ["The b-tagging algorithm used is the combined secondary vertex (Version 2). The performance at the medium operating point is approximately 10% tagging efficiency for c quark jets, 60% tagging efficiency for b quark jets, and a 1% misidentification probability for light jets.", "The b-tagging algorithm used is the combined secondary vertex (Version 2). The performance at the “medium” operating point is approximately 10% tagging efficiency for $\\mathup{{{c}}}$ quark jets, 60% tagging efficiency for $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ quark jets, and a 1% misidentification probability for light jets.", "The heavy-flavor tagging efficiencies for c and b jets are estimated in simulation and corrected by the efficiency scale factors. The systematic uncertainties of the efficiency scale factors of c jets and b jets with 30<p_T<100 GeV and |η|<2.4 are approximately 3.5% and 1.4%, respectively.", "The paper uses the combined secondary vertex (Version 2) algorithm for b-tagging. It operates at a “medium” working point with approximately 10% tagging efficiency for c quark jets, 60% for b quark jets, and a 1% misidentification probability for light jets.", "The systematic uncertainties of the efficiency scale factors of $\\mathup{{{c}}}$ jets and $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ jets with $30<p_{\\mathrm{T}}<100\\,\\text{Ge\\hskip-0.80002ptV}$ and $\\lvert\\eta\\rvert<2.4$ are ${\\approx}3.5\\%$ and ${\\approx}1.4\\%$ , respectively.", "The systematic uncertainties of the efficiency scale factors of c jets and b jets with 30<p_T<100 GeV and |η|<2.4 are approximately 3.5% and 1.4%, respectively.", "The text mentions a 'jet HF tagging requirement' but does not specify the algorithm or working point. It does provide scale factors for c and b jets, which are performance metrics: $\text{SF}_{\text{c}}=0.849\\pm 0.013\text{ (stat)}\\pm 0.064\text{ (syst)}$ and $\text{SF}_{\text{b}}=0.873\\pm 0.005\text{ (stat)}\\pm 0.013\text{ (syst)}$."], "votes": {"False": 23, "True": 7}, "escalated": false, "sections_read": [" + Abstract + Introduction + The CMS detector + Data and simulated samples", "Appendix B Measured differential cross section ratios", "Cross section ratio measurements + Analysis strategy + $\\mathup{{{Z}}}$ +HF jets event tagging efficiency", "Estimation of the event yields", "Object reconstruction and event selection", "Results + Summary + Appendix A Post-fit $M_{\\text{SV}}$ distributions in the exclusive jet $p_{\\mathrm{T}}$ bins", "Systematic uncertainties", "Unfolding"], "verdicts": [{"paper_id": "2001.06899", "qid": "gf-11", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Abstract + Introduction + The CMS detector + Data and simulated samples", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The question asks for the b-tagging algorithm, its working point, and its performance. The text does not explicitly mention a b-tagging algorithm, its working point, or its performance.\", \"quotes\": [], \"answer\": \"\", \"found\": false}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2001.06899", "qid": "gf-11", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Abstract + Introduction + The CMS detector + Data and simulated samples", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The text does not mention any b-tagging algorithm, working point, or performance.\",\n  \"quotes\": [],\n  \"answer\": \"\",\n  \"found\": false\n}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2001.06899", "qid": "gf-11", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Abstract + Introduction + The CMS detector + Data and simulated samples", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reas