jets.\",\n  \"found\": true\n}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2001.06899", "qid": "gf-11", "answer": true, "quote": "The discrimination of HF jets from light-flavor quark and gluon jets, referred to as light jets in the following, is achieved by constructing a discriminator variable from tracks and secondary vertex (SV) characteristics. Artificial neural network algorithms are used to combine specific properties of the HF quarks, long lifetime and substantial mass, to build the discriminator. The algorithm used in the analysis, the combined secondary vertex (Version 2), is described in Ref. [ 42 ] .", "quote_verified": true, "quotes": ["The discrimination of HF jets from light-flavor quark and gluon jets, referred to as light jets in the following, is achieved by constructing a discriminator variable from tracks and secondary vertex (SV) characteristics. Artificial neural network algorithms are used to combine specific properties of the HF quarks, long lifetime and substantial mass, to build the discriminator. The algorithm used in the analysis, the combined secondary vertex (Version 2), is described in Ref. [ 42 ] .", "The analysis uses a “medium” operating point, which corresponds to approximately 10 (60)% tagging efficiencies for $\\mathup{{{c}}}$ ( $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ ) quark jets and a misidentification probability of 1% for a light jet."], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "The paper uses the combined secondary vertex (Version 2) algorithm for b-tagging. It operates at a “medium” working point with approximately 10% tagging efficiency for c quark jets, 60% for b quark jets, and a 1% misidentification probability for light jets.", "section": "Object reconstruction and event selection", "window": 1, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The text mentions a b-tagging algorithm and its performance.\",\n  \"quotes\": [\n    \"The discrimination of HF jets from light-flavor quark and gluon jets, referred to as light jets in the following, is achieved by constructing a discriminator variable from tracks and secondary vertex (SV) characteristics. Artificial neural network algorithms are used to combine specific properties of the HF quarks, long lifetime and substantial mass, to build the discriminator. The algorithm used in the analysis, the combined secondary vertex (Version 2), is described in Ref. [ 42 ] .\",\n    \"The analysis uses a “medium” operating point, which corresponds to approximately 10 (60)% tagging efficiencies for $\\mathup{{{c}}}$ ( $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ ) quark jets and a misidentification probability of 1% for a light jet.\"\n  ],\n  \"answer\": \"The paper uses the combined secondary vertex (Version 2) algorithm for b-tagging. It operates at a “medium” working point with approximately 10% tagging efficiency for c quark jets, 60% for b quark jets, and a 1% misidentification probability for light jets.\",\n  \"found\": true\n}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2001.06899", "qid": "gf-11", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Object reconstruction and event selection", "window": 2, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The text does not mention any b-tagging algorithm, working point, or performance.\",\n  \"quotes\": [],\n  \"answer\": \"\",\n  \"found\": false\n}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2001.06899", "qid": "gf-11", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Object reconstruction and event selection", "window": 2, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The text does not mention any b-tagging algorithm, working point, or performance.\",\n  \"quotes\": [],\n  \"answer\": \"\",\n  \"found\": false\n}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2001.06899", "qid": "gf-11", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Object reconstruction and event selection", "window": 2, "escalated