{"paper_id": "2001.06899", "qid": "gf-11", "answer": true, "quote": "Heavy-flavor tagging efficiency: The HF tagging efficiencies for $\\mathup{{{c}}}$ and $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ jets are estimated in simulation and corrected by the efficiency scale factors as described in Section 5.2 . The systematic uncertainties of the efficiency scale factors of $\\mathup{{{c}}}$ jets and $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ jets with $30<p_{\\mathrm{T}}<100\\,\\text{Ge\\hskip-0.80002ptV}$ and $\\lvert\\eta\\rvert<2.4$ are ${\\approx}3.5\\%$ and ${\\approx}1.4\\%$ , respectively [ 42 ] .", "quote_verified": true, "quotes": ["Heavy-flavor tagging efficiency: The HF tagging efficiencies for $\\mathup{{{c}}}$ and $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ jets are estimated in simulation and corrected by the efficiency scale factors as described in Section 5.2 . The systematic uncertainties of the efficiency scale factors of $\\mathup{{{c}}}$ jets and $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ jets with $30<p_{\\mathrm{T}}<100\\,\\text{Ge\\hskip-0.80002ptV}$ and $\\lvert\\eta\\rvert<2.4$ are ${\\approx}3.5\\%$ and ${\\approx}1.4\\%$ , respectively [ 42 ] ."], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "The systematic uncertainties of the efficiency scale factors of c jets and b jets with 30<p_T<100 GeV and |η|<2.4 are approximately 3.5% and 1.4%, respectively.", "section": "Systematic uncertainties", "window": 7, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The text mentions heavy-flavor tagging efficiency and its uncertainties, but does not specify the b-tagging algorithm or its working point.\",\n  \"quotes\": [\n    \"Heavy-flavor tagging efficiency: The HF tagging efficiencies for $\\\\mathup{{{c}}}$ and $\\\\mathup{{{b}}}$ jets are estimated in simulation and corrected by the efficiency scale factors as described in Section 5.2 . The systematic uncertainties of the efficiency scale factors of $\\\\mathup{{{c}}}$ jets and $\\\\mathup{{{b}}}$ jets with $30<p_{\\\\mathrm{T}}<100\\\\,\\\\text{Ge\\\\hskip-0.80002ptV}$ and $\\\\lvert\\\\eta\\\\rvert<2.4$ are ${\\\\approx}3.5\\\\%$ and ${\\\\approx}1.4\\\\%$ , respectively [ 42 ] .\"\n  ],\n  \"answer\": \"The systematic uncertainties of the efficiency scale factors of c jets and b jets with 30<p_T<100 GeV and |η|<2.4 are approximately 3.5% and 1.4%, respectively.\",\n  \"found\": true\n}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2001.06899", "qid": "gf-11", "answer": true, "quote": "The HF tagging efficiencies for $\\mathup{{{c}}}$ and $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ jets are estimated in simulation and corrected by the efficiency scale factors as described in Section 5.2 .", "quote_verified": true, "quotes": ["The HF tagging efficiencies for $\\mathup{{{c}}}$ and $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ jets are estimated in simulation and corrected by the efficiency scale factors as described in Section 5.2 .", "The systematic uncertainties of the efficiency scale factors of $\\mathup{{{c}}}$ jets and $\\mathup{{{b}}}$ jets with $30<p_{\\mathrm{T}}<100\\,\\text{Ge\\hskip-0.80002ptV}$ and $\\lvert\\eta\\rvert<2.4$ are ${\\approx}3.5\\%$ and ${\\approx}1.4\\%$ , respectively [ 42 ] ."], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "The heavy-flavor tagging efficiencies for c and b jets are estimated in simulation and corrected by the efficiency scale factors. The systematic uncertainties of the efficiency scale factors of c jets and b jets with 30<p_T<100 GeV and |η|<2.4 are approximately 3.5% and 1.4%, respectively.", "section": "Systematic uncertainties", "window": 7, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text discusses systematic uncertainties in the analysis, including heavy-flavor tagging efficiency. It mentions the efficiency scale factors for c and b jets and their uncertainties, but does not specify the b-tagging algorithm or working point.\", \"quotes\": [\"The HF tagging efficiencies for $\\\\mathup{{{c}}}$ and $\\\\mathup{{{b}}}$ jets are estimated in simulation and corrected by the efficiency scale factors as described in Section 5.2 .\", \"The systematic uncertainties of the efficiency scale factor