he t2 mass or any specific mass limits.\",\n  \"quotes\": [],\n  \"answer\": \"\",\n  \"found\": false\n}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2006.05880", "qid": "gf-12", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Results", "window": 8, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The question asks for the observed 95% CL lower limit on the t2 mass in 2006.05880. The text discusses exclusion limits on the masses of the t1 and t2, but does not explicitly state the observed 95% CL lower limit on the t2 mass.\",\n  \"quotes\": [],\n  \"answer\": \"\",\n  \"found\": false\n}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2006.05880", "qid": "gf-12", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Results", "window": 8, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The text discusses exclusion limits on the masses of particles, including $\\tilde{t}_{1}$ and $\\tilde{\\chi}^{0}_{2}$, at 95% CL. It mentions specific mass ranges and conditions under which these limits are applied.\",\n  \"quotes\": [\n    \"For $\\tilde{\\chi}^{0}_{2}$ masses above 225 GeV , $\\tilde{t}_{1}$ masses up to about 1100 GeV are excluded at 95% CL, while $\\tilde{t}_{1}$ masses below 1220 GeV are excluded for a $\\tilde{\\chi}^{0}_{2}$ mass of 925 GeV .\",\n    \"The same statistical combination strategy is also used to obtain exclusion limits in the $\\tilde{t}_{1}\\to t\\tilde{\\chi}^{0}_{2}$ with $\\tilde{\\chi}^{0}_{2}\\to h/Z\\tilde{\\chi}^{0}_{1}$ simplified model for different $\\tilde{\\chi}^{0}_{2}\\to h/Z\\tilde{\\chi}^{0}_{1}$ decay branching ratios, shown in Figure 11 .\",\n    \"For $\\tilde{\\chi}^{0}_{2}$ masses above 300 GeV , the exclusion limits on $\\tilde{t}_{1}$ masses vary by at most 40 GeV depending on the $\\tilde{\\chi}^{0}_{2}\\to h/Z\\tilde{\\chi}^{0}_{1}$ branching ratios.\",\n    \"However, for $\\tilde{\\chi}^{0}_{2}$ masses below 200 GeV