{"qid": "gf-14", "paper_id": "2006.05880", "answer": true, "unanimous": false, "quote": "Searches for top squark production in events involving Higgs or $Z$ bosons have been performed previously by both ATLAS [ 20 , 21 ] and CMS [ 22 , 23 ] .", "all_quotes": ["Searches for top squark production in events involving Higgs or $Z$ bosons have been performed previously by both ATLAS [ 20 , 21 ] and CMS [ 22 , 23 ] .", "For each signal hypothesis, the background fit is repeated taking into account the signal contamination in the CRs, which is found to be below 12% for signal models close to the existing exclusion limits [ 20 ] .", "These results are obtained from the statistical combination of the shape-fit bins of SR ${}^{Z}_{1{\textrm{A}}}$ , SR ${}^{Z}_{1{\textrm{B}}}$ , SR ${}_{1{\textrm{A}}}^{h}$ , SR ${}_{1{\textrm{B}}}^{h}$ and SR ${}_{1{\textrm{AB}}}^{h}$ shown in Table 12 .", "These results improve upon the existing limits on the $\\tilde{t}_{1}$ mass in this model by approximately 300 GeV [ 20 ] .", "Results are compared with the observed limits obtained by the previous ATLAS search in Ref. [ 20 ] .", "Masses of the $\tilde{t}_{2}$ up to 875 GeV are excluded at 95% CL for a $\textstyle\tilde{\\chi}^{0}_{1}$ mass of about 350 GeV   and $\textstyle\tilde{\\chi}^{0}_{1}$ masses of approximately 520 (450) GeV are excluded for $\tilde{t}_{2}$ masses of 650 (800) GeV , extending beyond the previous limits on the $\textstyle\tilde{\\chi}^{0}_{1}$ mass from Ref. [ 89 ] by up to 160 GeV .", "Masses of the $\\tilde{t}_{2}$ up to 875 GeV are excluded at 95% CL for a $\\tilde{\\chi}^{0}_{1}$ mass of about 350 GeV \\ and $\\tilde{\\chi}^{0}_{1}$ masses of approximately 520 (450) GeV are excluded for $\\tilde{t}_{2}$ masses of 650 (800) GeV , extending beyond the previous limits on the $\\tilde{\\chi}^{0}_{1}$ mass from Ref. [ 89 ] by up to 160 GeV .", "Masses of the $\\tilde{t}_{2}$ up to 875 GeV are excluded at 95% CL for a $\\textstyle\\tilde{\\chi}^{0}_{1}$ mass of about 350 GeV   and $\\textstyle\\tilde{\\chi}^{0}_{1}$ masses of approximately 520 (450) GeV are excluded for $\\tilde{t}_{2}$ masses of 650 (800) GeV , extending beyond the previous limits on the $\\textstyle\\tilde{\\chi}^{0}_{1}$ mass from Ref. [ 89 ] by up to 160 GeV ."], "answers": ["The current analysis extends beyond the previous limits on the $\\tilde{\\chi}^{0}_{1}$ mass from Ref. [ 89 ] by up to 160 GeV.", "The new results extend beyond the previous limits on the $\\tilde{\\chi}^{0}_{1}$ mass from Ref. [ 89 ] by up to 160 GeV.", "The paper states that the $\textstyle\tilde{\\chi}^{0}_{1}$ mass limits extend beyond the previous limits from Ref. [ 89 ] by up to 160 GeV.", "The results improve upon the existing limits on the $\\tilde{t}_{1}$ mass in this model by approximately 300 GeV [ 20 ] . Results are compared with the observed limits obtained by the previous ATLAS search in Ref. [ 20 ] .", "The results improve upon the existing limits on the $\\tilde{t}_{1}$ mass in this model by approximately 300 GeV compared to the previous ATLAS search in Ref. [ 20 ] .", "The stop-mass limits in this analysis improve upon the existing limits on the $\\tilde{t}_{1}$ mass in this model by approximately 300 GeV compared to the previous ATLAS result.", "The text mentions that searches for top squark production in events involving Higgs or Z bosons have been performed previously by ATLAS.", "The text mentions that the signal contamination in the CRs is found to be below 12% for signal models close to the existing exclusion limits. It also discusses the statistical combination of shape-fit bins for deriving exclusion limits."], "votes": {"False": 61, "True": 8}, "escalated": false, "sections_read": [" + Introduction", "1 $\\ell$ selection + Background estimation", "3 $\\ell$ selection", "ATLAS detector + Data set and simulated event samples", "Conclusion", "Estimation of the $t\\bar{t}$ background in the 1 $\\ell$ selection + Systematic uncertainties", "Event selection", "Fake/n