{"qid": "gf-06", "paper_id": "2006.05880", "answer": true, "unanimous": false, "quote": "The events are classified into two exclusive categories: at least three leptons (referred to as 3 ℓ selection, aimed at top squark decays involving Z bosons), or exactly one lepton (referred to as 1 ℓ selection, aimed at top squark decays involving Higgs bosons). The selection requirements for each of these categories are described below.", "all_quotes": ["The events are classified into two exclusive categories: at least three leptons (referred to as 3 ℓ selection, aimed at top squark decays involving Z bosons), or exactly one lepton (referred to as 1 ℓ selection, aimed at top squark decays involving Higgs bosons). The selection requirements for each of these categories are described below.", "The observed number of events and expected yields are shown in Tables 10 and 11 for each of the inclusive 3 $\\ell$ and 1 $\\ell$ SRs, respectively.", "Table 10 also shows upper limits (at the 95% CL) on the number of BSM events $S^{95}$ , and on the visible BSM cross-section $\\sigma_{\\mathrm{vis}}=S_{\textrm{obs}}^{95}/\\int\\!{\\mathcal{}L}\textrm{d}t$ , defined as the product of the production cross-section, acceptance and efficiency.", "The observed number of events and expected yields in all these bins are shown in Figures 8 and 9 .", "Table 10: Observed and expected numbers of events in the 3 $\\ell$ signal regions.", "Table 11: Observed and expected numbers of events in the 1 $\\ell$ signal regions.", "These results are obtained from the statistical combination of the shape-fit bins of SR ${}^{Z}_{1{\textrm{A}}}$ , SR ${}^{Z}_{1{\textrm{B}}}$ , SR ${}_{1{\textrm{A}}}^{h}$ , SR ${}_{1{\textrm{B}}}^{h}$ and SR ${}_{1{\textrm{AB}}}^{h}$ shown in Table 12 .", "The bins of SR ${}_{1{\textrm{A}}}^{h}$ , SR ${}_{1{\textrm{B}}}^{h}$ and SR ${}_{1{\textrm{AB}}}^{h}$ are separately combined with the bins of SR ${}^{Z}_{1{\textrm{A}}}$ and SR ${}^{Z}_{1{\textrm{B}}}$ .", "These results are obtained from the statistical combination of SR ${}^{Z}_{2{\textrm{A}}}$ and the shape-fit bins of SR ${}^{Z}_{2{\textrm{B}}}$ shown in Table 12 ."], "answers": ["The 3 ℓ selection region requires at least three leptons and is aimed at top squark decays involving Z bosons.", "The text mentions several regions (SR ${}^{Z}_{1{\textrm{A}}}$ , SR ${}^{Z}_{1{\textrm{B}}}$ , SR ${}_{1{\textrm{A}}}^{h}$ , SR ${}_{1{\textrm{B}}}^{h}$ and SR ${}_{1{\textrm{AB}}}^{h}$) and their role in the statistical combination for obtaining results. It also mentions SR ${}^{Z}_{2{\textrm{A}}}$ and SR ${}^{Z}_{2{\textrm{B}}}$ in a different context.", "The text mentions several regions that require at least three leptons, including SR ${}^{Z}_{1{\textrm{A}}}$, SR ${}^{Z}_{1{\textrm{B}}}$, SR ${}^{Z}_{2{\textrm{A}}}$, and SR ${}^{Z}_{2{\textrm{B}}}$. These regions are used to set upper limits on the number of BSM events and the visible BSM cross-section. Additionally, the text discusses the use of these regions in the shape-fit approach to enhance the exclusion power in SUSY models. The role of each region is to provide data for the analysis, which is then used to derive exclusion limits and compare observed and expected event yields."], "votes": {"False": 64, "True": 5}, "escalated": false, "sections_read": [" + Introduction", "1 $\\ell$ selection + Background estimation", "3 $\\ell$ selection", "ATLAS detector + Data set and simulated event samples", "Conclusion", "Estimation of the $t\\bar{t}$ background in the 1 $\\ell$ selection + Systematic uncertainties", "Event selection", "Fake/non-prompt lepton background + Estimation of the $t\\bar{t}Z$ and multi-boson background in the 3 $\\ell$ selection", "Results"], "verdicts": [{"paper_id": "2006.05880", "qid": "gf-06", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Introduction", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The text does not mention any regions that require at least three leptons.\",\n  \"quotes\": [],\n  \"answer\": \"\",\n  \"found\": false\n}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2006.05880", "qid": "gf-06", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Introduction", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text discusses regions of the analysis that require at least three leptons, and the role each one plays.\", \"quotes\": [\"Unlike other top squark models, these signals can be efficiently distinguished from the SM top quark pair production ( $t\\bar{t}$ ) background by requiring either a same-flavour opposite-sign (SF-OS) lepton pair originating from the $Z\\to\\ell^{+}\\ell^{-}$ ( $\\ell\\equiv e,\\mu$ ) decay or a pair of $b$ -tagged jets originating from the $h\\to b\\bar{b}$ decay, plus the presence of an additional lepton produced in the decay of the top quarks in the event.\", \"The mass difference between the $\\tilde{t}_{1}$ and $\\textstyle\\tilde{\\chi}^{0}_{1}$ is set to be smaller than the $W$ boson mass, and the four-body decay $\\tilde{t}_{1}\\to bff^{\\prime}\\mathchoice{\\displaystyle\\raise 1.72218pt\\hbox{$\\displaystyle\\tilde{\\chi}^{0}_{1}$}}{\\textstyle\\raise 1.72218pt\\hbox{$\\textstyle\\tilde{\\chi}^{0}_{1}$}}{\\scriptstyle\\raise 0.90417pt\\hbox{$\\scriptstyle\\tilde{\\chi}^{0}_{1}$}}{\\scriptscriptstyle\\raise 0.64583pt\\hbox{$\\scriptscriptstyle\\tilde{\\chi}^{0}_{1}$}}$ is assumed to occur, where $f$ and $f^{\\prime}$ are two fermions from the $W^{*}$ decay, such as $\\tilde{t}_{1}\\to b\\ell\\nu\\mathchoice{\\displaystyle\\raise 1.72218pt\\hbox{$\\displaystyle\\tilde{\\chi}^{0}_{1}$}}{\\textstyle\\raise 1.72218pt\\hbox{$\\textstyle\\tilde{\\chi}^{0}_{1}$}}{\\scriptstyle\\raise 0.90417pt\\hbox{$\\scriptstyle\\tilde{\\chi}^{0}_{1}$}}{\\scriptscriptstyle\\raise 0.64583pt\\hbox{$\\scriptscriptstyle\\tilde{\\chi}^{0}_{1}$}}$.\"], \"answer\": \"The text mentions that signals can be distinguished from the SM top quark pair production background by requiring either a same-flavour"}, {"paper_id": "2006.05880", "qid": "gf-06", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": " + Introduction", "window": 0, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The text does not mention any regions that require at least three leptons.\",\n  \"quotes\": [],\n  \"answer\": \"\",\n  \"found\": false\n}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2006.05880", "qid": "gf-06", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "ATLAS detector + Data set and simulated event samples", "window": 1, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The text does not mention any regions that require at least three leptons or the role they play.\",\n  \"quotes\": [],\n  \"answer\": \"\",\n  \"found\": false\n}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2006.05880", "qid": "gf-06", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "ATLAS detector + Data set and simulated event samples", "window": 1, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The text does not mention any regions that require at least three leptons or the role of such regions.\",\n  \"quotes\": [],\n  \"answer\": \"\",\n  \"found\": false\n}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2006.05880", "qid": "gf-06", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "No information found.", "section": "ATLAS detector + Data set and simulated event samples", "window": 1, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text does not mention any regions that require at least three leptons or the role of any regions.\", \"quotes\": [], \"answer\": \"No information found.\", \"found\": false}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2006.05880", "qid": "gf-06", "answer": true, "quote": "The events are classified into two exclusive categories: at least three leptons (referred to as 3 ℓ selection, aimed at top squark decays involving Z bosons), or exactly one lepton (referred to as 1 ℓ selection, aimed at top squark decays involving Higgs bosons). The selection requirements for each of these categories are described below.", "quote_verified": true, "quotes": ["The events are classified into two exclusive categories: at least three leptons (referred to as 3 ℓ selection, aimed at top squark decays involving Z bosons), or exactly one lepton (referred to as 1 ℓ selection, aimed at top squark decays involving Higgs bosons). The selection requirements for each of these categories are described below."], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "The 3 ℓ selection region requires at least three leptons and is aimed at top squark decays involving Z bosons.", "section": "Event selection", "window": 2, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The text mentions regions that require at least three leptons and describes their roles.\",\n  \"quotes\": [\n    \"The events are classified into two exclusive categories: at least three leptons (referred to as 3 ℓ selection, aimed at top squark decays involving Z bosons), or exactly one lepton (referred to as 1 ℓ selection, aimed at top squark decays involving Higgs bosons). The selection requirements for each of these categories are described below.\"\n  ],\n  \"answer\": \"The 3 ℓ selection region requires at least three leptons and is aimed at top squark decays involving Z bosons.\",\n  \"found\": true\n}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2006.05880", "qid": "gf-06", "answer": true, "quote": "The events are classified into two exclusive categories: at least three leptons (referred to as 3 ℓ selection, aimed at top squark decays involving Z bosons), or exactly one lepton (referred to as 1 ℓ selection, aimed at top squark decays involving Higgs bosons).", "quote_verified": true, "quotes": ["The events are classified into two exclusive categories: at least three leptons (referred to as 3 ℓ selection, aimed at top squark decays involving Z bosons), or exactly one lepton (referred to as 1 ℓ selection, aimed at top squark decays involving Higgs bosons)."], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "The 3 ℓ selection region requires at least three leptons and is aimed at top squark decays involving Z bosons.", "section": "Event selection", "window": 2, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The text mentions regions that require at least three leptons and describes the role of these regions.\",\n  \"quotes\": [\n    \"The events are classified into two exclusive categories: at least three leptons (referred to as 3 ℓ selection, aimed at top squark decays involving Z bosons), or exactly one lepton (referred to as 1 ℓ selection, aimed at top squark decays involving Higgs bosons).\"\n  ],\n  \"answer\": \"The 3 ℓ selection region requires at least three leptons and is aimed at top squark decays involving Z bosons.\",\n  \"found\": true\n}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2006.05880", "qid": "gf-06", "answer": true, "quote": "The events are classified into two exclusive categories: at least three leptons (referred to as 3 ℓ selection, aimed at top squark decays involving Z bosons), or exactly one lepton (referred to as 1 ℓ selection, aimed at top squark decays involving Higgs bosons).", "quote_verified": true, "quotes": ["The events are classified into two exclusive categories: at least three leptons (referred to as 3 ℓ selection, aimed at top squark decays involving Z bosons), or exactly one lepton (referred to as 1 ℓ selection, aimed at top squark decays involving Higgs bosons)."], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "The 3 ℓ selection region requires at least three leptons and is aimed at top squark decays involving Z bosons.", "section": "Event selection", "window": 2, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The text mentions regions that require at least three leptons and describes their role.\",\n  \"quotes\": [\n    \"The events are classified into two exclusive categories: at least three leptons (referred to as 3 ℓ selection, aimed at top squark decays involving Z bosons), or exactly one lepton (referred to as 1 ℓ selection, aimed at top squark decays involving Higgs bosons).\"\n  ],\n  \"answer\": \"The 3 ℓ selection region requires at least three leptons and is aimed at top squark decays involving Z bosons.\",\n  \"found\": true\n}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2006.05880", "qid": "gf-06", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "3 $\\ell$ selection", "window": 3, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The text mentions regions that require at least three leptons and describes the role of some of these regions.\",\n  \"quotes\": [\n    \"The presence of at least three signal leptons (electrons or muons, referred to collectively with the symbol $\\\\ell$ ), with at least one SF-OS lepton pair whose invariant mass is compatible with the $Z$ boson mass ( $|m_{\\\\ell\\\\ell}-m_{Z}|<15$ GeV , with $m_{Z}=91.2$ GeV ) is required.\",\n    \"Four overlapping signal regions (SRs) are optimised for the best discovery sensitivity, two for each of the simplified models described in Section Introduction .\",\n    \"Signal region SR ${}^{Z}_{1{\\\\textrm{A}}}$ is optimised for large $\\\\mathchoice{\\\\displaystyle\\\\raise 1.72218pt\\\\hbox{\\\\displaystyle\\\\tilde{\\\\chi}^{0}_{2}}}{\\\\textstyle\\\\raise 1.72218pt\\\\hbox{\\\\textstyle\\\\tilde{\\\\chi}^{0}_{2}}}{\\\\scriptstyle\\\\raise 0.90417pt\\\\hbox{\\\\scriptstyle\\\\tilde{\\\\chi}^{0}_{2}}}{\\\\scriptscriptstyle\\\\raise 0.64583pt\\\\hbox{\\\\scriptscriptstyle\\\\tilde{\\\\chi}^{0}_{2}}}$-\\\\mathchoice{\\\\displaystyle\\\\raise 1.72218pt\\\\hbox{\\\\displaystyle\\\\tilde{\\\\chi}^{0}_{1}}}{\\\\textstyle\\\\raise 1.72218pt\\\\hbox{\\\\textstyle\\\\tilde{\\\\chi}^{0}_{1}}}{\\\\scriptstyle\\\\raise 0.90417pt\\\\hbox{\\\\scriptstyle\\\\tilde{\\\\chi}^{0}_{1}}}{\\\\scriptscriptstyle\\\\raise 0.64583pt\\\\hbox{\\\\scriptscriptstyle\\\\tilde{\\\\chi}^{0}_{1}}}$ mass splittings in the $\\\\tilde{t}_{1}\\\\to t\\\\mathchoice{\\\\displaystyle\\\\raise 1.72218pt\\\\hbox{\\\\displaystyle\\\\tilde{\\\\chi}^{0}_{2}}}{\\\\textstyle\\\\raise 1.72218pt\\\\hbox{\\\\textstyle\\\\tilde{\\\\chi"}, {"paper_id": "2006.05880", "qid": "gf-06", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "3 $\\ell$ selection", "window": 3, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The text mentions regions that require at least three leptons and describes the role of some of these regions.\",\n  \"quotes\": [\n    \"The presence of at least three signal leptons (electrons or muons, referred to collectively with the symbol $\\ell$ ), with at least one SF-OS lepton pair whose invariant mass is compatible with the $Z$ boson mass ( $|m_{\\ell\\ell}-m_{Z}|<15$ GeV , with $m_{Z}=91.2$ GeV ) is required.\",\n    \"Four overlapping signal regions (SRs) are optimised for the best discovery sensitivity, two for each of the simplified models described in Section Introduction .\",\n    \"Signal region SR ${}^{Z}_{1{\\textrm{A}}}$ is optimised for large $\\mathchoice{\\displaystyle\\raise 1.72218pt\\hbox{$\\displaystyle\\tilde{\\chi}^{0}_{2}$}}{\\textstyle\\raise 1.72218pt\\hbox{$\\textstyle\\tilde{\\chi}^{0}_{2}$}}{\\scriptstyle\\raise 0.90417pt\\hbox{$\\scriptstyle\\tilde{\\chi}^{0}_{2}$}}{\\scriptscriptstyle\\raise 0.64583pt\\hbox{$\\scriptscriptstyle\\tilde{\\chi}^{0}_{2}$}}-\\mathchoice{\\displaystyle\\raise 1.72218pt\\hbox{$\\displaystyle\\tilde{\\chi}^{0}_{1}$}}{\\textstyle\\raise 1.72218pt\\hbox{$\\textstyle\\tilde{\\chi}^{0}_{1}$}}{\\scriptstyle\\raise 0.90417pt\\hbox{$\\scriptstyle\\tilde{\\chi}^{0}_{1}$}}{\\scriptscriptstyle\\raise 0.64583pt\\hbox{$\\scriptscriptstyle\\tilde{\\chi}^{0}_{1}$}}$ mass splittings in the $