\\hbox{$\\scriptscriptstyle\\tilde{\\chi}^{0}_{2}$}}$"}, {"paper_id": "2006.05880", "qid": "gf-06", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "1 $\\ell$ selection + Background estimation", "window": 4, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The text does not mention any regions that require at least three leptons.\",\n  \"quotes\": [],\n  \"answer\": \"\",\n  \"found\": false\n}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2006.05880", "qid": "gf-06", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "1 $\\ell$ selection + Background estimation", "window": 4, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The text does not mention any regions that require at least three leptons.\",\n  \"quotes\": [],\n  \"answer\": \"\",\n  \"found\": false\n}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2006.05880", "qid": "gf-06", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "1 $\\ell$ selection + Background estimation", "window": 4, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The text does not mention any regions that require at least three leptons.\",\n  \"quotes\": [],\n  \"answer\": \"\",\n  \"found\": false\n}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2006.05880", "qid": "gf-06", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Fake/non-prompt lepton background + Estimation of the $t\\bar{t}Z$ and multi-boson background in the 3 $\\ell$ selection", "window": 5, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The text discusses regions that require at least three leptons and their roles in the analysis.\",\n  \"quotes\": [\n    \"Two VRs are defined as detailed in Table 4 , with VR ${}^{Z}_{1{\\textrm{F}}}$ probing the lepton $p_{\\text{T}}$ regime in SR ${}^{Z}_{1{\\textrm{A}}}$ and SR ${}^{Z}_{1{\\textrm{B}}}$ , while VR ${}^{Z}_{2\\textrm{F}}$ includes soft lepton requirements as in SR ${}^{Z}_{2{\\textrm{A}}}$ and SR ${}^{Z}_{2{\\textrm{B}}}$ .\",\n    \"Requirement / Region VR ${}^{Z}_{1{\\textrm{F}}}$ VR ${}^{Z}_{2\\textrm{F}}$ Number of signal leptons $\\geq 3$\",\n    \"To ensure mutual exclusion with the SRs, only events with $50\\penalty 10000\\ \\text{Ge\\kern-1.00006ptV}\\ <E_{\\text{T}}^{\\text{miss}}<100$ GeV are included in CR ${}^{Z}_{t\\bar{t}Z}$ , while a $b$ -tagged jet veto and a $50\\penalty 10000\\ \\text{Ge\\kern-1.00006ptV}\\ <E_{\\text{T}}^{\\text{miss}}<200$ GeV requirement are applied in CR ${}^{Z}_{VV}$ .\",\n    \"Requirement / Region CR ${}^{Z}_{t\\bar{t}Z}$ VR ${}^{Z}_{t\\bar{t}Z}$ CR ${}^{Z}_{VV}$ VR ${}_{VV}^{Z\\textrm{,n-jet}}$ VR ${}_{VV}^{Z\\textrm{,}b\\textrm{-tag}}$ Number of signal leptons $\\geq 3$\",\n    \"The VR ${}^{Z}_{t\\bar{t}Z}$ region primarily validates the $t\\bar{t}Z$ background estimate. The VR ${}_{VV}^{Z\\textrm{,n-jet}}$ and VR ${}_{VV}^{Z\\textrm{,}b\\textrm{-tag}}$ regions validate the multi-boson background estimate, the former focusing on the extrapolation in jet multiplicity and the latter releasing the $b$ -tagged jet veto.\""}, {"paper_id": "2006.05880", "qid": "gf-06", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Fake/non-prompt lepton background + Estimation of the $t\\bar{t}Z$ and multi-boson background in the 3 $\\ell$ selection", "window": 5, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The text touches on the regions that require at least three leptons and their roles.\",\n  \"quotes\": [\n    \"Two VRs are defined as detailed in Table 4 , with VR ${}^{Z}_{1{\\textrm{F}}}$ probing the lepton $p_{\\text{T}}$ regime in SR ${}^{Z}_{1{\\textrm{A}}}$ and SR ${}^{Z}_{1{\\textrm{B}}}$ , while VR ${}^{Z}_{2\\textrm{F}}$ includes soft lepton requirements as in SR ${}^{Z}_{2{\\textrm{A}}}$ and SR ${}^{Z}_{2{\\textrm{B}}}$ .\",\n    \"The two dedicated control regions used for the $t\\bar{t}Z$ (CR ${}^{Z}_{t\\bar{t}Z}$ ) and multi-boson (CR ${}^{Z}_{VV}$ ) background estimation in the 3 $\\ell$ selection are defined in Table 6 .\",\n    \"The VR ${}^{Z}_{t\\bar{t}Z}$ region primarily validates the $t\\bar{t}Z$ background estimate.\",\n    \"The VR ${}_{VV}^{Z\\textrm{,n-jet}}$ and VR ${}_{VV}^{Z\\textrm{,}b\\textrm{-tag}}$ regions validate the multi-boson background estimate, the former focusing on the extrapolation in jet multiplicity and the latter releasing the $b$ -tagged jet veto.\"\n  ],\n  \"answer\": \"The regions VR ${}^{Z}_{1{\\textrm{F}}}$ and VR ${}^{Z}_{2\\textrm{F}}$ are defined with selection criteria similar to those defining the 3 $\\ell$ SRs but with reduced contributions from processes with three prompt leptons. VR ${}^{Z}_{1{\\textrm{F}}}$ probes the lepton $p_{\\text{T}}$ regime in SR ${}^{Z}_{1{\\textrm{A}}}$ and SR ${}^{Z}_{1{\\textrm{B}}}$ , while VR ${}^{Z}_{2\\textrm{F}}$ includes soft lepton requirements as in SR ${}^{Z}_{2{\\textrm{A}}}$ and SR ${}^{Z}_{2{\\textrm{B}}}$ . The control regions CR ${}^{Z}_{t\\bar{t}Z}$ and CR ${}^{Z}_{VV}$ are used for the $t\\bar{t}Z$ and multi-boson background estimation in the 3 $\\ell$ selection. The VR ${"}, {"paper_id": "2006.05880", "qid": "gf-06", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Fake/non-prompt lepton background + Estimation of the $t\\bar{t}Z$ and multi-boson background in the 3 $\\ell$ selection", "window": 5, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The text mentions several regions that require at least three leptons and describes their roles.\",\n  \"quotes\": [\n    \"Two VRs are defined as detailed in Table 4 , with VR ${}^{Z}_{1{\\textrm{F}}}$ probing the lepton $p_{\\text{T}}$ regime in SR ${}^{Z}_{1{\\textrm{A}}}$ and SR ${}^{Z}_{1{\\textrm{B}}}$ , while VR ${}^{Z}_{2\\textrm{F}}$ includes soft lepton requirements as in SR ${}^{Z}_{2{\\textrm{A}}}$ and SR ${}^{Z}_{2{\\textrm{B}}}$ .\",\n    \"To enhance fakes and be mutually exclusive with the SR, events in these VRs are required to have no SF-OS dilepton pairs and to have at least one different-flavour opposite-sign (DF-OS) dilepton pair.\",\n    \"The two dedicated control regions used for the $t\\bar{t}Z$ (CR ${}^{Z}_{t\\bar{t}Z}$ ) and multi-boson (CR ${}^{Z}_{VV}$ ) background estimation in the 3 $\\ell$ selection are defined in Table 6 .\",\n    \"To validate the background estimates and provide a statistically independent cross-check of the extrapolation to the SRs, three validation regions are defined, as shown in Table 6 . The VR ${}^{Z}_{t\\bar{t}Z}$ region primarily validates the $t\\bar{t}Z$ background estimate. The VR ${}_{VV}^{Z\\textrm{,n-jet}}$ and VR ${}_{VV}^{Z\\textrm{,}b\\textrm{-tag}}$ regions validate the multi-boson background estimate, the former focusing on the extrapolation in jet multiplicity and the latter releasing the $b$ -tagged jet veto.\"\n  ],\n  \"answer\": \"The regions VR ${}^{Z}_{1{\\textrm{F}}}$ and VR ${}^{Z}_{2\\textrm{F}}$ require at least three leptons and are used to probe different lepton $p_{\\text{T}}$ regimes and soft lepton requirements. The control regions CR ${}^{Z}_{t\\bar{t}Z}$ and CR ${}^{Z}_{VV}$ also require at least three leptons and are used for background estimation. The validation regions VR ${}^{Z}_{t\\bar{t}Z}$, VR ${}_{VV}^{Z\\textrm{,"}, {"paper_id": "2006.05880", "qid": "gf-06", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Estimation of the $t\\bar{t}$ background in the 1 $\\ell$ selection + Systematic uncertainties", "window": 6, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The text does not mention any regions that require at least three leptons.\",\n  \"quotes\": [],\n  \"answer\": \"\",\n  \"found\": false\n}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2006.05880", "qid": "gf-06", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Estimation of the $t\\bar{t}$ background in the 1 $\\ell$ selection + Systematic uncertainties", "window": 6, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The text does not mention any regions that require at least three leptons, nor does it specify the role of any such regions.\",\n  \"quotes\": [],\n  \"answer\": \"\",\n  \"found\": false\n}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2006.05880", "qid": "gf-06", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Estimation of the $t\\bar{t}$ background in the 1 $\\ell$ selection + Systematic uncertainties", "window": 6, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The text does not mention regions that require at least three leptons, nor does it discuss the role of any regions.\",\n  \"quotes\": [],\n  \"answer\": \"\",\n  \"found\": false\n}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2006.05880", "qid": "gf-06", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Results", "window": 7, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The text touches on the regions that require at least three leptons and the role each one plays.\",\n  \"quotes\": [\n    \"The observed number of events and expected yields are shown in Tables 10 and 11 for each of the inclusive 3 $\\ell$ and 1 $\\ell$ SRs, respectively.\",\n    \"Table 10 also shows upper limits (at the 95% CL) on the number of BSM events $S^{95}$ , and on the visible BSM cross-section $\\sigma_{\\mathrm{vis}}=S_{\\textrm{obs}}^{95}/\\int\\!{\\mathcal{}L}\\textrm{d}t$ , defined as the product of the production cross-section, acceptance and efficiency.\",\n    \"Table 10: Observed and expected numbers of events in the 3 $\\ell$ signal regions. The pre-fit predictions from MC simulation are given for comparison for those backgrounds ( $t\\bar{t}Z$ , multi-boson) that are normalised to data in dedicated control regions.\",\n    \"SR ${}^{Z}_{1{\\textrm{A}}}$ is used in the exclusion fits with no changes.\",\n    \"The observed number of events and expected yields in all these bins are shown in Figures 8 and 9 .\",\n    \"Table 12 shows the definition of these bins, which loosen a few of the requirements of the discovery SRs to increase the acceptance for different classes of models across the phase space (Tables 2 and 3 ).\",\n    \"The bins of SR ${}_{1{\\textrm{A}}}^{h}$ , SR ${}_{1{\\textrm{B}}}^{h}$ and SR ${}_{1{\\textrm{AB}}}^{h}$ are separately combined with the bins of SR ${}^{Z}_{1{\\textrm{A}}}$ and SR ${}^{Z}_{1{\\textrm{B}}}$ .\",\n    \"These results are obtained from the statistical combination of the shape-fit bins of SR ${}^{Z}_{1{\\textrm{A}}}$ , SR ${}^{Z}_{1{\\textrm{B}}}$ , SR ${}_{1{\\textrm{A}}}^{h}$ , SR ${}_{1{\\textrm{B}}}^{h}$ and SR ${}_{1{\\textrm{AB}}}^{h}$ shown in Table 12 .\"\n  ],\n  \"answer\": \"The regions that require at least three leptons are SR ${}^{Z}_{"}, {"paper_id": "2006.05880", "qid": "gf-06", "answer": true, "quote": "The observed number of events and expected yields are shown in Tables 10 and 11 for each of the inclusive 3 $\\ell$ and 1 $\\ell$ SRs, respectively.", "quote_verified": true, "quotes": ["The observed number of events and expected yields are shown in Tables 10 and 11 for each of the inclusive 3 $\\ell$ and 1 $\\ell$ SRs, respectively.", "Table 10 also shows upper limits (at the 95% CL) on the number of BSM events $S^{95}$ , and on the visible BSM cross-section $\\sigma_{\\mathrm{vis}}=S_{\textrm{obs}}^{95}/\\int\\!{\\mathcal{}L}\textrm{d}t$ , defined as the product of the production cross-section, acceptance and efficiency.", "The observed number of events and expected yields in all these bins are shown in Figures 8 and 9 .", "The observed number of events and expected yields are shown in Tables 10 and 11 for each of the inclusive 3 $\\ell$ and 1 $\\ell$ SRs, respectively.", "Table 10: Observed and expected numbers of events in the 3 $\\ell$ signal regions.", "Table 11: Observed and expected numbers of events in the 1 $\\ell$ signal regions."], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "The text mentions several regions that require at least three leptons, including SR ${}^{Z}_{1{\textrm{A}}}$, SR ${}^{Z}_{1{\textrm{B}}}$, SR ${}^{Z}_{2{\textrm{A}}}$, and SR ${}^{Z}_{2{\textrm{B}}}$. These regions are used to set upper limits on the number of BSM events and the visible BSM cross-section. Additionally, the text discusses the use of these regions in the shape-fit approach to enhance the exclusion power in SUSY models. The role of each region is to provide data for the analysis, which is then used to derive exclusion limits and compare observed and expected event yields.", "section": "Results", "window": 7, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The text touches on the regions that require at least three leptons and the role each one plays.\",\n  \"quotes\": [\n    \"The observed number of events and expected yields are shown in Tables 10 and 11 for each of the inclusive 3 $\\ell$ and 1 $\\ell$ SRs, respectively.\",\n    \"Table 10 also shows upper limits (at the 95% CL) on the number of BSM events $S^{95}$ , and on the visible BSM cross-section $\\sigma_{\\mathrm{vis}}=S_{\\textrm{obs}}^{95}/\\int\\!{\\mathcal{}L}\\textrm{d}t$ , defined as the product of the production cross-section, acceptance and efficiency.\",\n    \"The observed number of events and expected yields in all these bins are shown in Figures 8 and 9 .\",\n    \"The observed number of events and expected yields are shown in Tables 10 and 11 for each of the inclusive 3 $\\ell$ and 1 $\\ell$ SRs, respectively.\",\n    \"Table 10: Observed and expected numbers of events in the 3 $\\ell$ signal regions.\",\n    \"Table 11: Observed and expected numbers of events in the 1 $\\ell$ signal regions.\"\n  ],\n  \"answer\": \"The text mentions several regions that require at least three leptons, including SR ${}^{Z}_{1{\\textrm{A}}}$, SR ${}^{Z}_{1{\\textrm{B}}}$, SR ${}^{Z}_{2{\\textrm{A}}}$, and SR ${}^{Z}_{2{\\textrm{B}}}$. These regions are used to set upper limits on the number of BSM events and the visible BSM cross-section. Additionally, the text discusses the use of these regions in the shape-fit approach to enhance the exclusion power in SUSY models. The role of each region is to provide data for the analysis, which is then used to derive exclusion limits and compare observed and expected event yields.\",\n  \"found\": true\n}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2006.05880", "qid": "gf-06", "answer": null, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Results", "window": 7, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The text mentions several regions that require at least three leptons and provides details about their roles.\",\n  \"quotes\": [\n    \"The observed number of events and expected yields are shown in Tables 10 and 11 for each of the inclusive 3 $\\ell$ and 1 $\\ell$ SRs, respectively.\",\n    \"Table 10 also shows upper limits (at the 95% CL) on the number of BSM events $S^{95}$ , and on the visible BSM cross-section $\\sigma_{\\mathrm{vis}}=S_{\\textrm{obs}}^{95}/\\int\\!{\\mathcal{}L}\\textrm{d}t$ , defined as the product of the production cross-section, acceptance and efficiency.\",\n    \"To enhance the exclusion power in the SUSY models considered, a ‘shape-fit’ approach is used where several mutually exclusive bins in different kinematic variables are defined in order to take advantage of the different signal-to-background ratios in the different bins. Table 12 shows the definition of these bins, which loosen a few of the requirements of the discovery SRs to increase the acceptance for different classes of models across the phase space (Tables 2 and 3 ). SR ${}^{Z}_{2{\\textrm{A}}}$ is used in the exclusion fits with no changes.\",\n    \"The observed number of events and expected yields in all these bins are shown in Figures 8 and 9 .\",\n    \"The ‘Others’ category contains the contributions from $t\\bar{t}h$ , $t\\bar{t}W$ , $t\\bar{t}WW$ , $t\\bar{t}t$ , $t\\bar{t}t\\bar{t}$ , $Wh$ , and $Zh$ production.\",\n    \"The ‘FNP’ category represents the background from fake or non-prompt leptons.\",\n    \"The expected distributions for selected signal models are also shown as dashed lines.\",\n    \"The last bin in each figure contains the overflow.\",\n    \"The ‘Higgs’ category contains the contributions from gluon–gluon fusion, vector-boson fusion, $Wh$ , $Zh$ and $t\\bar{t}h$ production.\",\n    \"The ‘Others’ category contains the contributions from $t\\bar{t}WW$ , $t\\bar{t}WZ$ , $t\\bar{t}t$ and $t\\bar{t}t\\bar{t}$"}, {"paper_id": "2006.05880", "qid": "gf-06", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Results", "window": 8, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The text mentions several regions (SRs) but does not specify which require at least three leptons. It does not provide the role each region plays.\",\n  \"quotes\": [],\n  \"answer\": \"\",\n  \"found\": false\n}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2006.05880", "qid": "gf-06", "answer": false, "quote": "", "quote_verified": false, "quotes": [], "reasoning": "", "answer_text": "", "section": "Results", "window": 8, "escalated": false, "raw": "```json\n{\"reasoning\": \"The text mentions several regions but does not specify which ones require at least three leptons or the role each one plays.\", \"quotes\": [], \"answer\": \"\", \"found\": false}\n```"}, {"paper_id": "2006.05880", "qid": "gf-06", "answer": true, "quote": "These results are obtained from the statistical combination of the shape-fit bins of SR ${}^{Z}_{1{\textrm{A}}}$ , SR ${}^{Z}_{1{\textrm{B}}}$ , SR ${}_{1{\textrm{A}}}^{h}$ , SR ${}_{1{\textrm{B}}}^{h}$ and SR ${}_{1{\textrm{AB